==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-single point of failure.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|single points of failure}}

# A [[component]] in a [[device]], or a point in a [[network]], that, if it were to [[fail]], would cause the entire device or network to fail (normally eliminated by adding [[redundancy]]).
#: The [[Jesus nut]] got its name because it was a '''single point of failure'''- if it went, there was nothing you could do but pray.
#: {{syn|en|SPF|SPOF}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A minor mistake that creates a [[chain reaction]].
#: {{ux|en|The [[intact]] [[twine]] in Dylan's [[beef Wellington]] was a '''single point of failure'''.}}

